[2026-01-30T17:02:35.570Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Badges Are A Type System In Disguise\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: functionality\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: insight_synth\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:23:42 AM\n\n## Description\nTypeBadge, SourceTypeBadge, ConfidenceBadge, CredibilityBadge, PriorityBadge, StatusBadge all map a domain value to a visual representation. Create a BadgeSchema system where badges are defined declaratively: { domain: 'findingType', values: { fact: { color: 'indigo', label: 'Fact' }}}. Generate badge components from schemas.\n\n## Reasoning\nSix badge components with identical structure but different color mappings is a maintenance burden. A schema-driven approach would make adding new badge types trivial, ensure consistency, and enable dynamic badge generation for user-defined categories.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Theming & Cards\n\n**Description**: Themed UI components for reports: stat cards, sections, badges, and core elements. Includes animated numbers and theme context for consistent styling.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/ThemedCards.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/core/ThemeContext.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/core/AnimatedNumber.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/core/index.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/Cards.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/Badges.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/ProgressBar.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/Icons.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\n- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb700aba-f9fc-4283-93cf-561e37220b63","uuid":"662e2283-a608-42b2-b49d-095e2064227d","isSynthetic":true}
